What is a Turbine Disk?
Turbine disks are critical rotating components in gas turbines that support and fix turbine blades to the rotor shaft. These high-performance disks must withstand extreme thermal and mechanical stresses from high-temperature gas flows and rotational speeds exceeding 10,000 RPM. Acting as hot-end components, their material properties and manufacturing precision directly impact turbine efficiency and operational reliability in demanding aerospace and industrial applications.
Functioning at the core of turbine engines, these components are strategically positioned to endure immense centrifugal forces while maintaining structural integrity under continuous high-stress operating conditions.
